{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Digital twin Project, Driven occupancy demand\n","\n","---\n","\n","## 1. Title & Final Introduction\n","\n","### 1.1 Project Title\n","**An End-to-End Predictive Pipeline for Titanic Passenger Survival: Benchmarking Tree-Based Ensembles, Connectionist Models, and Meta-Learning Frameworks with Post-Hoc Probability Calibration.**\n","\n","### 1.2 Team Members & Final Roles\n","\n","*   **[Joko Wasono]**: **Data Preprocessing & Advanced Feature Engineering Lead (M1).** Engineered the master data manipulation block, deployed regular expressions for title grouping, isolated localized sub-deck categorical arrays, and structured the unified `ColumnTransformer` platform to guarantee reproducible data streams without structural leakage.\n","*   **[Anggi Arrivian]**: **Parametric Baseline & Logistic Regression Specialist (M2).** Formulated and integrated the initial parametric linear classification baseline, monitored standard feature scaling metrics, and computed early model coefficients to measure baseline demographic weights.\n","*   **[Wisnu Wibowo]**: **Iterative Machine Learning & Decision Tree Analyst (M3).** Researched localized decision boundaries, mapped baseline non-linear tree splits, and evaluated data impurity reductions to establish a theoretical foundation for complex tree-based systems.\n","*   **[Yudhistira]**: **Hyperparameter Optimization & Random Forest Ensemble Engineer (M4).** Commanded the parallel tree ensemble modeling track, configured multi-tree decision boundaries, and executed exhaustive 5-fold cross-validated grid sweeps (`GridSearchCV`) to locate optimized parameter paths.\n","*   **[Wisnu Wibowo]**: **Connectionist Systems & Deep Learning Specialist (M5).** Designed, structured, and trained the connectionist Artificial Neural Network (`MLPClassifier`) framework, configuring dual hidden-layer dimensions (64 and 32 neurons) backed by ReLU activation functions and Adam solvers.\n","*   **[Wisnu Wibowo]**: **Model Evaluation, Synthesis, Meta-Learning & Pipeline Integration Lead (M6).** Built the comprehensive multi-metric evaluation table, consolidated base estimators into a soft-voting meta-ensemble consensus grid, deployed post-hoc Isotonic probability calibrations, and calibrated classification thresholds via F1-score optimization curves.\n","\n","### 1.3 Project Overview & Objectives\n","This project develops a highly robust, fully reproducible data science workflow utilizing the official historical passenger manifest of the RMS Titanic. Moving beyond simple classification exercises, this project treats predictive modeling as a rigorous analytical exploration.\n","\n","The primary objectives of this study are to:\n","1. Construct an automated, end-to-end engineering pipeline that cleans and converts raw historical data into optimized modeling vectors.\n","2. Benchmark traditional linear estimators against parallel tree ensembles, sequential tree gradient boosters, connectionist deep learning structures, and meta-learning frameworks.\n","3. Quantify the real-world operational reliability of models using post-hoc probability calibration, log-loss stability profiling, and threshold optimization.\n","\n","\n","**Workflow Mapping (Notebook Steps):**\n","\n","*   **Step 1:** Initialization and environment setup (Importing foundational data science libraries and loading the raw passenger manifest data).\n","\n","*   **Step 2:** Establishing the analytical framework (Defining the problem context, historical boundary constraints, and baseline goals for the predictive pipeline).\n","\n","---"],"metadata":{"id":"wkhS0mwdupwI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 2. Dataset Overview & Updated Narrative\n","\n","### 2.1 Dataset Description & Feature Overview (Revisited)\n","* **Source & Scale:** The dataset consists of 891 individual passenger profiles (rows) tracking 12 structural baseline attributes from the official maritime manifest of the RMS Titanic.\n","* **Engineered Feature Suite:** To decode complex social nuances, our workflow engineered several key socio-behavioral features during the deep data preparation phase:\n","    * `Title`: Grouped prefix designations (Mr, Mrs, Miss, Master, Rare) extracted via RegEx to evaluate social hierarchy and kasta strings.\n","    * `Deck`: Passenger room location mappings derived from the first letter of the raw `Cabin` parameter.\n","    * `FamilySize` & `IsAlone`: Domestically contextual metrics combining sibling/spouse and parent/child counts to evaluate evacuation dynamics.\n","    * `FarePerPerson`: An adjusted economic baseline isolating individual wealth from multi-passenger ticket groups.\n","    * `TicketGroupSize`: Co-traveler size calculations mapped from shared ticket frequencies.\n","    * `AgeGroup`: Categorical age bands segmentation ('Child', 'Young Adult', 'Adult', 'Senior').\n","\n","### 2.2 Revised Data Questions & Narrative Integration\n","\n","#### EDA-Related Questions (Descriptive Analysis)\n","1. *How did systemic socio-economic status stratifications and the strict enforcement of the \"women and children first\" maritime protocol structurally impact descriptive survival distributions?*\n","2. *Does the continuous correlation grid reveal robust linear relationships among raw ticket pricing vectors and engineered familial sizes?*\n","\n","#### ML-Related Questions (Predictive Modeling)\n","3. *Can non-linear tree ensembles and deep connectionist models successfully uncover localized non-linear survival boundaries that traditional parametric classifiers fail to isolate?*\n","4. *Which engineered features carry the most significant decision weight when models are aggregated into an ensemble consensus system?*"],"metadata":{"id":"o7K3tm6_u8vx"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 3. Complete Data Science Workflow\n","\n","### 3.1 Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n","Our final descriptive diagnostics verify that `Sex` and `Pclass` acted as the primary systemic filters during the disaster. The continuous correlation matrix exhibits a powerful inverse relationship between `Pclass` and `Survived` (-0.34), proving that lower-class passengers faced severe structural bottlenecks and geographical isolation from lifeboat decks. Conversely, `Fare` maintains a robust positive correlation with survival (0.26) , mathematically demonstrating the life-saving impact of socio-economic priority and financial privilege.\n","\n","* **Workflow Mapping (Notebook Steps):**\n","    * **Step 3:** Structural integrity exploration, dimensional assessment (`df.shape`), and baseline statistical data type distributions.\n","    * **Step 4:** Comprehensive visual data storytelling utilizing demographic class counts (`Survival by Gender`, `Survival by Class`) and a linear correlation matrix heatmap.\n","\n","### 3.2 Data Cleaning & Preprocessing\n","* **Imputation Strategy:** Missing values within the categorical `Embarked` attribute are resolved via mode imputation (filling gaps with the most frequent entry). Continuous gaps within the `Age` feature are handled dynamically by computing the localized median age of passengers sharing the exact same social `Title`.\n","* **Feature Engineering:** To prevent data leakage during split validation, all custom variables are engineered dynamically within our pipeline architecture. Family structure dynamics are captured through the following mathematical formulation:\n","$$\\text{FamilySize} = \\text{SibSp} + \\text{Parch} + 1$$\n","* **Preprocessing Pipeline Automation:** We deployed a unified `ColumnTransformer` system to process heterogeneous data streams simultaneously. Categorical markers are transformed into sparse numerical vectors via `OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore')`, while continuous numerical fields are scaled using `StandardScaler` to enforce a uniform variance distribution across all modelling inputs[cite: 137].\n","\n","* **Workflow Mapping (Notebook Steps):**\n","    * **Step 5:** Advanced Feature Engineering (RegEx extraction for `Title` sub-groups, mapping physical deck arrays from `Cabin` prefixes, calculating unified `FamilySize`, and formulating `FarePerPerson`).\n","    * **Step 6 & Step 7:** High-dimensional null isolation, missing value processing, and the explicit structural decoupling of feature space matrices (`X`) from target vectors (`y`).\n","    * **Step 8:** Building the automated data transformation pipeline using Scikit-Learn’s `ColumnTransformer` and `Pipeline` wrappers.\n","\n","### 3.3 Model Development, Training, and Evaluation\n","\n","#### Modeling Approach\n","Five distinct algorithmic architectures are trained and evaluated side-by-side to thoroughly benchmark the boundaries of predictive capability across the decision space:\n","1. **Logistic Regression:** Serving as our classical, parametric linear baseline model.\n","2. **Random Forest:** A parallel decision tree ensemble engineered to maximize accuracy and depress model variance.\n","3. **XGBoost:** A sequential tree gradient booster focused on systematically minimizing residual optimization errors.\n","4. **Neural Network (MLP):** A multi-layered connectionist network mapping highly intricate, non-linear feature interactions using two hidden layers (configured with 64 and 32 neurons) running on ReLU activation functions.\n","5. **Voting Classifier:** A collaborative meta-ensemble aggregating baseline model outputs using soft probability consensus weights to achieve peak prediction stability.\n","\n","#### Training, Tuning, and Post-Hoc Calibration\n","All models are optimized using cross-validated sweeps to ensure strict generalization capabilities. The Random Forest configurations were resolved using a 5-fold cross-validated grid search (`GridSearchCV`), while the XGBoost parameters were refined via Bayesian Optimization using the `Optuna` engine over 30 evaluation trials.\n","\n","To ensure our probability distributions reflect honest, trustworthy real-world risk profiles rather than overconfident guesses, all baseline estimators are encapsulated and calibrated using `CalibratedClassifierCV` via the Isotonic method. Finally, classification thresholds are empirically optimized to maximize the F1-Score.\n","\n","* **Workflow Mapping (Notebook Steps):**\n","    * **Step 9:** Baseline linear model instantiation, coefficient extraction, and training (`Logistic Regression`).\n","    * **Step 10:** Connectionist network implementation (`MLPClassifier`) and the creation of multi-stage meta-estimators (`StackingClassifier`).\n","    * **Step 11 & Step 12:** Advanced hyperparameter tuning execution utilizing exhaustive grid sweeps (`GridSearchCV`) and Bayesian optimization loops (`Optuna`).\n","    * **Step 13:** Consolidating predictive power into a unified soft-voting ensemble consensus grid (`VotingClassifier`).\n","    * **Step 14:** Production-ready model serialization and artifact exporting (`titanic_best_model.pkl`) via the `pickle` framework.\n","    * **Step 15:** Comprehensive multi-metric performance evaluation, model benchmarking, and tabular reporting.\n","    * **Step 16:** Post-hoc probability calibration curves deployment and threshold alignment analysis."],"metadata":{"id":"phav_pFPvusZ"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"metadata":{"id":"E9F2h34lR_7m","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787530798252,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":7466,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}},"outputId":"1bb7f0f5-4d79-478c-f381-268f72278fdd"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Mounted at /content/MyDrive\n"]}],"source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/content/MyDrive')"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{"id":"eh9O8UcXSQFv","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":397},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787530805977,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":2588,"user":{"displayName":"Wis