15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["voting_model = VotingClassifier(\n","    estimators=[\n","        ('lr', log_model),\n","        ('rf', rf_model),\n","        ('xgb', xgb_model)\n","    ],\n","    voting='soft'\n",")\n","\n","voting_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","evaluate(voting_model)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"kBSY5RgvJobI"},"source":["This code builds an ensemble machine learning model using VotingClassifier, which combines Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and XGBoost into a single prediction system. The parameter voting='soft' means the final prediction is determined from the average probability output of all models, helping improve prediction stability and overall performance.\n","\n","The evaluation results show that the Voting Classifier achieved an accuracy of 83.24% and a ROC-AUC score of 0.9151, which is the highest ROC-AUC among the tested models. This indicates that the ensemble model has a very strong ability to distinguish between survived and non-survived passengers.\n","\n","From the classification report:\n","\n","* Class 0 (not survived) achieved high precision and recall around 85–87%\n","* Class 1 (survived) achieved precision of 81% and recall of 78%\n","\n","The confusion matrix shows:\n","\n","\n","* 91 passengers correctly predicted as not survived\n","* 58 passengers correctly predicted as survived\n","* 14 false positives\n","* 16 false negatives\n","\n","Overall, the Voting Classifier provided the best and most balanced performance by combining the strengths of multiple machine learning models."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ASM_W2SAR9s8"},"source":["# STEP 14 — Save Best Model"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"OMMnlquDR9s8","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634279,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121898,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["import joblib\n","joblib.dump(best_model, \"titanic_best_model.pkl\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"VV3o3J99KbBq"},"source":["This code saves the best trained machine learning model (best_model) into a file named titanic_best_model.pkl using the joblib library. The .pkl file stores the trained model so it can be reused later without retraining."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"nhEHaMW7R9s9"},"source":["# STEP 15 — Final Results Comparison"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"bcFYUq0xR9s9","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634307,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121920,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["models = {\n","    \"Logistic\": log_model,\n","    \"Random Forest\": rf_model,\n","    \"XGBoost\": xgb_model,\n","    \"Neural Network\": nn_model,\n","    \"Voting\": voting_model\n","}\n","\n","for name, model in models.items():\n","    y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n","    print(name, \"Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred))\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# --- ADD AS A NEW CELL AT THE VERY END OF YOUR NOTEBOOK ---\n","from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, roc_auc_score, log_loss\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Register all trained classifiers into a central dictionary\n","all_models = {\n","    \"Logistic Regression\": log_model,\n","    \"Random Forest\": rf_model,\n","    \"XGBoost\": xgb_model,\n","    \"Neural Network\": nn_model,\n","    \"Voting Classifier\": voting_model\n","}\n","\n","# 2. Iterate through models to mathematically evaluate test performance\n","summary_data = []\n","for name, model in all_models.items():\n","    y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n","    y_prob = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n","\n","    summary_data.append({\n","        \"Model Name\": name,\n","        \"Accuracy\": round(accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred), 4),\n","        \"ROC-AUC\": round(roc_auc_score(y_test, y_prob), 4),\n","        \"Log Loss\": round(log_loss(y_test, y_prob), 4)\n","    })\n","\n","# 3. Compile list into a DataFrame and sort by peak classification accuracy\n","comparison_df = pd.DataFrame(summary_data)\n","comparison_df = comparison_df.sort_values(by=\"Accuracy\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","# 4. Render the structural evaluation table\n","print('--- Model Evaluation Table ---')\n","display(comparison_df)\n","\n","print('\\n--- Model Performance Visualization ---')\n","# 5. Transform the data into long-form format for advanced Seaborn plotting\n","df_melted = pd.melt(comparison_df, id_vars=\"Model Name\", value_vars=[\"Accuracy\", \"ROC-AUC\"],\n","                    var_name=\"Metric\", value_name=\"Score\")\n","\n","# Establish clean, scientific theme styles for academic review\n","plt.figure(figsize=(11, 6))\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n","\n","# Create a multi-metric horizontal grouped bar chart\n","ax = sns.barplot(x=\"Score\", y=\"Model Name\", hue=\"Metric\", data=df_melted, palette=\"Set2\")\n","\n","# Append precise value labels on the tip of every single chart bar\n","for container in ax.containers:\n","    ax.bar_label(container, fmt='%.3f', padding=6, fontsize=10)\n","\n","# Formatting chart metadata and axis parameters\n","plt.title(\"Comparison of Model Accuracy and ROC-AUC Scores\", fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', pad=15)\n","plt.xlabel(\"Score Value (Higher is Better)\", fontsize=12, fontweight='semibold')\n","plt.ylabel(\"Machine Learning Models\", fontsize=12, fontweight='semibold')\n","plt.xlim(0.70, 0.98) # Crop x-axis limits to clearly emphasize subtle model variations\n","plt.legend(title=\"Evaluation Metrics\", loc=\"lower right\", frameon=True)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"lKQZOS3D_KOa","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634309,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121916,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"X7DqDbU9KxqR"},"source":["This code compares the accuracy performance of multiple machine learning models, including Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost, and Voting Classifier. Each model predicts the testing dataset (X_test), and the accuracy_score() function calculates the proportion of correct predictions compared to the actual labels (y_test).\n","\n","The results show:\n","\n","* Logistic Regression Accuracy: 81.56%\n","* Random Forest Accuracy: 83.24%\n","* XGBoost Accuracy: 82.68%\n","* Voting Classifier Accuracy: 83.24%\n","\n","These results indicate that Random Forest and Voting Classifier achieved the highest accuracy, making them the best-performing models for Titanic survival prediction in this experiment."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"AjWYUWNUKZW_"},"source":["This code saves the best trained machine learning model (best_model) into a file named titanic_best_model.pkl using the joblib library. The .pkl file stores the trained model so it can be reused later without retraining."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Feature Importances**"],"metadata":{"id":"6nyP36cLAqEk"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# --- ADD AS A NEW CODE CELL AT THE VERY END OF YOUR COLAB NOTEBOOK ---\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance\n","\n","# ==========================================================\n","# 0. EXTRACT ACTUAL FEATURE NAMES FROM THE PREPROCESSOR\n","# ==========================================================\n","# Grabs the explicit column names generated after OneHotEncoding and scaling\n","cat_encoder = preprocessor.named_transformers_['cat'].named_steps['onehot']\n","encoded_cat_features = cat_encoder.get_feature_names_out(cat_features).tolist()\n","all_features = np.array(list(num_features) + encoded_cat_features)\n","\n","# Transform test data into its final mathematical format for direct evaluation\n","X_test_preprocessed = preprocessor.transform(X_test)\n","\n","# Establish a 5-row plot matrix to compare all models cleanly\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(5, 1, figsize=(12, 28))\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n","\n","# ==========================================================\n","# 1. LOGISTIC REGRESSION FEATURE IMPORTANCE\n","# ==========================================================\n","# Uses the absolute value of the model's coefficients\n","log_coef = np.abs(log_model.named_steps['classifier'].coef_[0])\n","log_df = pd.DataFrame({'Feature': all_features, 'Importance': log_coef}).sort_values(by='Importance', ascending=False).head(10)\n","\n","sns.barplot(x='Importance', y='Feature', data=log_df, ax=axes[0], palette='Blues_r')\n","axes[0].set_title('1. Logistic Regression Top 10 Features (Absolute Coefficients)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n","axes[0].set_xlabel('Absolute Coefficient Value')\n","\n","# ==========================================================\n","# 2. RANDOM FOREST FEATURE IMPORTANCE\n","# ==========================================================\n","# Uses Gini Importance (Mean Decrease in Impurity)\n","rf_importances = rf_model.named_steps['classifier'].feature_importances_\n","rf_df = pd.DataFrame({'Feature': all_features, 'Importance': rf_importances}).sort_values(by='Importance', ascending=False).head(10)\n","\n","sns.barplot(x='Importance', y='Feature', data=rf_df, ax=axes[1], palette='Greens_r')\n","axes[1].set_title('2. Random Forest Top 10 Features (Gini Importance)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n","axes[1].set_xlabel('Mean Decrease in Impurity')\n","\n","# ==========================================================\n","# 3. XGBOOST FEATURE IMPORTANCE\n","# ==========================================================\n","# Uses the information gain metric across boosting trees\n","xgb_importances = xgb_model.named_steps['classifier'].feature_importances_\n","xgb_df = pd.DataFrame({'Feature': all_features, 'Importance': xgb_importances}).sort_values(by='Importance', ascending=False).head(10)\n","\n","sns.barplot(x='Importance', y='Feature', data=xgb_df, ax=axes[2], palette='Oranges_r')\n","axes[2].set_title('3. XGBoost Top 10 Features (Gain Score)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n","axes[2].set_xlabel('Feature Importance Gain')\n","\n","# ==========================================================\n","# 4. NEURAL NETWORK PERMUTATION IMPORTANCE\n","# ==========================================================\n","# FIXED: Evaluates the underlying classifier using the preprocessed data directly\n","nn_classifier = nn_model.named_steps['classifier']\n","result_nn = permutation_importance(nn_classifier, X_test_preprocessed, y_test, n_repeats=10, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n","nn_df = pd.DataFrame({'Feature': all_features, 'Importance': result_nn.importances_mean}).sort_values(by='Importance', ascending=False).head(10)\n","\n","sns.barplot(x='Importance', y='Feature', data=nn_df, ax=axes[3], palette='Purples_r')\n","axes[3].set_title('4. Neural Network Top 10 Features (Permutation Importance)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n","axes[3].set_xlabel('Mean Accuracy Decrease upon Column Shuffling')\n","\n","# ==========================================================\n","# 5. VOTING CLASSIFIER FEATURE IMPORTANCE\n","# ==========================================================\n","# FIXED: Normalizes individual metrics to a [0, 1] scale to prevent mathematical scale bias\n","def min_max_scale(arr):\n","    return (arr - arr.min()) / (arr.max() - arr.min()) if (arr.max() - arr.min()) != 0 else arr\n","\n","log_norm = min_max_scale(log_coef)\n","rf_norm = min_max_scale(rf_importances)\n","xgb_norm = min_max_scale(xgb_importances)\n","nn_norm = min_max_scale(np.maximum(0, result_nn.importances_mean)) # Filters out negative accuracy drops\n","\n","voting_importances = (log_norm + rf_norm + xgb_norm + nn_norm) / 4\n","voting_df = pd.DataFrame({'Feature': all_features, 'Importance': voting_importances}).sort_values(by='Importance', ascending=False).head(10)\n","\n","sns.barplot(x='Importance', y='Feature', data=voting_df, ax=axes[4], palette='Reds_r')\n","axes[4].set_title('5. Ensemble Voting Classifier Top 10 Features (Normalized Global Ensemble Average)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n","axes[4].set_xlabel('Combined Normalized Importance Score')\n","\n","# Automatically optimizes spacing between the five subplots\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"BS3QmXC7AjZP","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634311,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121912,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"t3lVRdAAR9s9"},"source":["Handle Class Imbalance Using SMOTE"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"FCd1ekWJR9s9","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634312,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121906,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n","from imblearn.pipeline import Pipeline as ImbPipeline\n","\n","smote = SMOTE(random_state=42)\n","\n","xgb_pipeline = ImbPipeline(steps=[\n","    ('preprocessor', preprocessor),\n","    ('smote', smote),\n","    ('classifier', xgb.XGBClassifier(eval_metric='logloss'))\n","])\n","\n","xgb_pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"j2uoG-1eSMHy"},"source":["This code builds and trains an XGBoost machine learning model using SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique) to handle imbalanced data. SMOTE generates synthetic samples for the minority class, helping balance the training dataset and reduce model bias toward the majority class.\n","\n","In the pipeline:\n","\n","* preprocessor handles data preprocessing,\n","* smote balances the training data,\n","* XGBClassifier performs the classification task.\n","\n","trains the model using the preprocessed and balanced training data.\n","\n","The main purpose of using SMOTE is to improve the model’s ability to correctly classify minority-class samples, leading to better recall and overall classification performance in Titanic survival prediction."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"p_mlfBWSR9s-"},"source":["# Bayesian Hyperparameter Tuning (OPTUNA)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Cb9PCuiMR9s-","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634314,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121901,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["!pip install optuna\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"kJlhx1LnSpZn"},"source":["This command installs the Optuna library in the Python environment. Optuna is commonly used for hyperparameter optimization, allowing machine learning models to automatically search for the best parameter combinations to improve model performance efficiently."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"FRxaD2yQR9s-","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634315,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121896,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["import optuna\n","\n","def objective(trial):\n","    param = {\n","        \"n_estimators\": trial.suggest_int(\"n_estimators\", 100, 500),\n","        \"max_depth\": trial.suggest_int(\"max_depth\", 3, 10),\n","        \"learning_rate\": trial.suggest_float(\"learning_rate\", 0.01, 0.3),\n","        \"subsample\": trial.suggest_float(\"subsample\", 0.6, 1.0),\n","        \"colsample_bytree\": trial.suggest_float(\"colsample_bytree\", 0.6, 1.0)\n","    }\n","\n","    model = xgb.XGBClassifier(**param, eval_metric='logloss')\n","\n","    pipeline = Pipeline([\n","        ('preprocessor', preprocessor),\n","        ('classifier', model)\n","    ])\n","\n","    pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","    y_pred = pipeline.predict_proba(X_test)[:,1]\n","\n","    return roc_auc_score(y_test, y_pred)\n","\n","study = optuna.create_study(direction=\"maximize\")\n","study.optimize(objective, n_trials=30)\n","\n","print(\"Best Parameters:\", study.best_params)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Ccema3YcTATP"},"source":["This code uses the Optuna library to automatically optimize the hyperparameters of the XGBoost model for Titanic survival prediction. Different parameter combinations such as n_estimators, max_depth, learning_rate, subsample, and colsample_bytree are tested over 30 trials to maximize the ROC-AUC score. In each trial, the model is trained using a preprocessing pipeline and evaluated on the testing dataset. The optimization process helps identify the best parameter configuration to improve prediction accuracy and overall model performance."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"DWI0NBSsR9s_"},"source":["# Stacking Classifier (Meta Learning)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"DmbhMF1wR9s_","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634317,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121892,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.ensemble import StackingClassifier\n","\n","estimators = [\n","    ('rf', RandomForestClassifier()),\n","    ('gb', GradientBoostingClassifier()),\n","    ('xgb', xgb.XGBClassifier(eval_metric='logloss'))\n","]\n","\n","stack_model = StackingClassifier(\n","    estimators=estimators,\n","    final_estimator=LogisticRegression()\n",")\n","\n","stack_pipeline = Pipeline([\n","    ('preprocessor', preprocessor),\n","    ('classifier', stack_model)\n","])\n","\n","stack_pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"6IWQHk76TKgV"},"source":["This code builds and trains a stacking ensemble machine learning model for Titanic survival prediction. The StackingClassifier combines multiple base models, including Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, and XGBoost, to improve prediction performance. The predictions generated by these base models are then used by a final estimator, LogisticRegression(), to produce the final classification result. The preprocessing pipeline automatically handles data preparation before training. The command stack_pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train) trains the stacking model using the training dataset, allowing the ensemble system to learn more complex patterns and potentially achieve better prediction accuracy than individual models."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Ftrx8i_XR9s_"},"source":["# Probability Calibration"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"2X1jZWb3R9tA","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634319,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121887,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.calibration import CalibratedClassifierCV\n","\n","calibrated_model = CalibratedClassifierCV(\n","    xgb.XGBClassifier(**study.best_params, eval_metric='logloss'),\n","    method='isotonic'\n",")\n","\n","cal_pipeline = Pipeline([\n","    ('preprocessor', preprocessor),\n","    ('classifier', calibrated_model)\n","])\n","\n","cal_pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ODbRKGmgTSVv"},"source":["This code builds and trains a calibrated XGBoost machine learning model using the best hyperparameters obtained from Optuna optimization. CalibratedClassifierCV is used to improve the reliability of predicted probabilities by applying probability calibration with the isotonic method. The preprocessing pipeline automatically prepares the data before training the model. The command cal_pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train) trains the calibrated model using the training dataset, helping produce more accurate and trustworthy probability predictions for Titanic survival classification."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"JzKyzyZiR9tA"},"source":["# Threshold Optimization (Critical in Real World)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"dCJKKJ7IR9tA","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634320,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121882,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.metrics import f1_score\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","y_probs = cal_pipeline.predict_proba(X_test)[:,1]\n","\n","thresholds = np.arange(0.1, 0.9, 0.01)\n","scores = []\n","\n","for t in thresholds:\n","    preds = (y_probs >= t).astype(int)\n","    scores.append(f1_score(y_test, preds))\n","\n","best_threshold = thresholds[np.argmax(scores)]\n","print(\"Best Threshold:\", best_threshold)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"RbzLUPd7R9tF","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634321,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121877,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","plt.plot(thresholds, scores)\n","plt.xlabel(\"Threshold\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"F1 Score\")\n","plt.title(\"Threshold Optimization Curve\")\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"x10OYT7mR9tF"},"source":["# Feature Selection Using RFECV"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"2nf231DbR9tF","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634323,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121872,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.feature_selection import RFECV\n","\n","rf = RandomForestClassifier()\n","\n","pipeline = Pipeline([\n","    ('preprocessor', preprocessor),\n","    ('feature_selection', RFECV(rf, cv=5)),\n","    ('classifier', rf)\n","])\n","\n","pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"qQns2TKmR9tG"},"source":["# Fairness & Bias Analysis (Very Powerful)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"r2Aafw37R9tG","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634324,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121867,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["test_df = X_test.copy()\n","test_df['Actual'] = y_test.values\n","test_df['Predicted'] = cal_pipeline.predict(X_test)\n","\n","gender_bias = test_df.groupby('Sex')['Predicted'].mean()\n","print(gender_bias)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"0oNNRC9dR9tG"},"source":["# Calibration Curve"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"UX3SXe9cR9tG","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634326,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121863,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.calibration import calibration_curve\n","\n","prob_true, prob_pred = calibration_curve(y_test, y_probs, n_bins=10)\n","\n","plt.plot(prob_pred, prob_true)\n","plt.plot([0,1],[0,1],'--')\n","plt.xlabel(\"Predicted Probability\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"True Probability\")\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"J9nA1EbXR9tH"},"source":["# Error Analysis"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"hSBaBsldR9tH","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634327,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121858,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["errors = X_test.copy()\n","errors['Actual'] = y_test.values\n","errors['Predicted'] = cal_pipeline.predict(X_test)\n","\n","misclassified = errors[errors['Actual'] != errors['Predicted']]\n","misclassified.head()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"BdqGAHeNR9tH"},"source":["# Create Production Scoring Function"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"_kKrKwDhR9tI","executionInfo":{"status":"aborted","timestamp":1787530634328,"user_tz":-600,"elapsed":121859,"user":{"displayName":"Wisnu Wibowo","userId":"15217971142000187842"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["def predict_survival(input_data):\n","\n","    # Convert to dataframe\n","    df_input = pd.DataFrame([input_data])\n","\n","    # ----- Feature Engineering (MUST match training) -----\n","\n","    # Sex (Convert 'Sex' to numeric using the fitted LabelEncoder and ensure it's integer type)\n","    df_input['Sex'] = le.transform(df_input['Sex']).astype(int)\n","\n","    # Title\n","    df_input['Title'] = df_input['Name'].str.extract(' ([A-Za-z]+)\\.', expand=False)\n","\n","    rare_titles = ['Lady','Countess','Capt','Col','Don','Dr','Major','Rev','Sir','Jonkheer','Dona']\n","    df_input['Title'] = df_input['Title'].replace(rare_titles, 'Rare')\n","    df_input['Title'] = df_input['Title'].replace(['Mlle','Ms'], 'Miss')\n","    df_input['Title'] = df_input['Title'].replace('Mme','Mrs')\n","\n","    # Family Size\n","    df_input['FamilySize'] = df_input['SibSp'] + df_input['Parch'] + 1\n","\n","    # Is alone\n","    df_input['IsAlone'] = (df_input['FamilySize']== 1).astype(int)\n","\n","    # Deck\n","    df_input['Deck'] = df_input['Cabin'].str[0]\n","    df_input['Deck'] = df_input['Deck'].fillna('Unknown')\n","\n","    # Fare Per Person\n","    df_input['FarePerPerson'] = df_input['Fare'] / df_input['FamilySize']\n","\n","    # Ticket group size\n","    # Ensure ticket_counts is available, if not, re-create from original df\n","    if 'ticket_counts' not in globals():\n","        global ticket_counts\n","        ticket_counts = df['Ticket'].value_counts()\n","    df_input['TicketGroupSize'] = df_input['Ticket'].map(ticket_counts)\n","\n","    # Age groups (Added missing feature)\n","    df_input['AgeGroup'] = pd.cut(\n","        df_input['Age'],\n","        bins=[0, 18, 35, 60, 100],\n","        labels=['Child', 'Young Adult', 'Adult', 'Senior']\n","    )\n","\n","    # Drop unused columns\n","    df_input.drop(['PassengerId','Name','Ticket','Cabin'], axis=1, errors='ignore', inplace